      "coverage": "arXiv:1507.02341v3, arXiv:2206.07561v1 and arXiv:2407.03309v1 read in full; arXiv:2103.00647 pages 5 to 12; Graham and Lovász (1978) pages 60 to 67 and 80 to 86; nine web queries (peak location with double star, caterpillar, diameter, 2023 to 2026) and two citation lists. In these sources the peak is located only for stars and paths (Collins, as cited), and the only general bounds are Theorems 3.3 and 3.6 of arXiv:1507.02341; for a double star Theorem 3.6 gives ⌊(n − 2)/4⌋.",
